// ACME Unified P&L - Power BI vs the vosk.dev web report: golden answers and engine reference outputs.
// Oracle: .sync/pnl/report-spec/08-validation.md (vosk.dev, 2026-11-16): §2 the 63 golden answers (expected values at full
// precision from C:\__VOSK__\data\pnl\checks\chat-golden.csv) and §4 the web engine's outputs for the default views.
// Spec measure names are mapped to this model's names (gap doc §11 D9: no renames, no wrappers); the cut is set on the
// parameter tables exactly as the report's slicers set it; Column = Budget / Prior year = param_eval CMP_A with
// param_compare_a B / PY.
// Tolerances. Goldens (chat-metrics.test.ts): amounts 0.011, counts 0, ratios / per-unit 1e-9, each + |expected| x 1e-9.
// §4 tables printed to cents / 6 dp: 0.016 / 5.1e-7. §4 display texts ($ m 1 dp, % 1 dp, pp 1 dp): half a display unit.
// Default view (§4): FY 2026, Sep, Year to date, base Actual, Compare A Budget, Compare B Prior year, USD, actual rates.
// Known data-layer drift (gap doc §1): fact_pl_allocated is cent-rounded with a residual; rows that combine a channel /
// line / segment slice with a below-CM line can miss by up to ~1 currency unit until the loader writes unrounded shares
// (D6, ginee). Tagged (a) on 2026-11-16, fail until lh_raw / the pack Parquet are reloaded with the unrounded allocation:
// G-22 (OP, line HOME, diff 0.24), G-27 (NP, segment PREM, diff 0.66), G-62 (EBITDA share, segment SMB, diff 4.7e-9).
// Phase 2 (layout, 2026-11-16): block R-15 covers header / period / statement texts, display switches, custom range (RANGE), variance filter texts
// and trend rows; n.m. is covered by the R-05 / R-06 variance rows (LV Δ % Text).
// Block R-16 (2026-11-16): the bridges' static label formats (USD millions) on the chart's bar values against the 08 §4.3 Label column.
// Run one EVALUATE at a time in DAX query view (or per block over ADOMD); every row must show _pass = TRUE.

EVALUATE
